Package: pamflow
Title: End-to-End Passive Acoustic Monitoring Workflow
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Pradeeshwar", family = "Rajagopal James",
    email = "pradeeshwarrj@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1246-442X"))
Description: Tools for passive acoustic monitoring projects, from raw recordings
    to data ready for ecological analysis. Standardizes and checks field
    recordings, runs 'BirdNET' through its Python package, cleans and validates
    detections, and computes soundscape indices. Builds detection histories,
    count histories and input for occupancy and abundance models, summarizes
    activity patterns and species richness, and writes HTML, PDF and Excel
    reports. Optional Shiny apps support standardization, validation and
    annotation, and the training of custom 'BirdNET' classifiers.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
SystemRequirements: FFmpeg (audio conversion, filtering and clips); uv (creates
    the optional Python environment for 'BirdNET')
